                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/597b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-25T17:00:00-05:00">April 25, 1935—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Your service message with regard to Department’s 63. Groups as received
                    correct. The thought Department meant to convey in next to the last paragraph
                    was that the satisfactoriness of the method now being considered for dealing
                    with this question would naturally depend on the actual details of the
                    unilateral plan developed by the Brazilian Government. These should meet all
                    reasonable tests of fairness and feasibility.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
